schema: test/v2
level: working-unit
epic: E-UIINSPECT
wu: E-UIINSPECT.W2
tests:
  unit:
    count: 12
    what: "ui/src/flow.test.ts (extends the toRow/statusTone suite): bodyText decodes captured base64 as UTF-8 (héllo) and returns empty for non-captured legs; toCurl omits -X for GET and shell-quotes url + each header, adds -X METHOD + --data-raw for a captured request body, and escapes embedded single quotes via the '\'' idiom. ui/src/FlowDetail.test.tsx: loading notice until the flow arrives; the panel renders request line/status(text-ok)/timing/versions(HTTP/1.1 -> HTTP/2.0)/both header tables/curl from a fixture; the copy button calls navigator.clipboard.writeText with the curl and flips to copied; the close button fires onClose."
  integration:
    count: 2
    what: "ui/src/App.test.tsx (RTL over the mock TrawlerApi): (1) clicking a flow row calls getFlow(id) and opens the detail panel rendering the fetched flow uri + a curl line reflecting its headers; (2) regression for the review fix — after copying curl for one flow, selecting a different row resets the copy button (no stale copied state), proving the key={selectedId} remount. Wires selection -> useFlowDetail -> FlowDetail -> Layout.detail against the typed client. Full vitest suite 23 green; tsc -b and pnpm build clean."
  e2e:
    waived: "W2 adds the detail chrome but not the body viewers; the epic e2e (UC-5) is carried by W3, which drives the real Tauri window (click row -> detail: headers/timing/versions, curl text asserted in the DOM per the plan curl waiver). W2 is proven at the unit + integration (RTL) layers here; no window-level behavior lands until W3 mounts the body viewers."
